  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "deps",
      "claim": "go.mod moves llmgw-core from v0.14.0 to v0.14.1, whose only change makes the Copilot vertical forward the gateway transport's full Chat field list.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/go.mod; llmgw-core v0.14.1 release notes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "copilot-through-runtime",
      "claim": "GitHub Copilot Chat, Responses and both streams go through the llmgw-core Runtime with core's Copilot vertical, built from the gateway's shared copilot client, integration ID, editor version and adaptation setting. Credentials resolve as before: a human's own connection then legacy credential, a service or system caller's project binding, and the gateway-wide token when the caller has no principal. copilotAuth, the OpenAIAuth refresh hooks and the transport's Copilot 401 replay branches are removed; console login flows and SetCopilotEndpointsForTests are unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/copilot_vertical.go, openai.go, openai_auth.go; go/internal/api/testdata unchanged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "parity",
      "claim": "Upstream Copilot request bytes are unchanged, including parallel_tool_calls, stream_options and thinking on the Messages-to-Chat path; copilotGuidance messages are kept; a Responses 404 or 405 still triggers the Chat fallback; the X-LLMGW-Adapted header is set exactly when Chat is served over Responses; the catalog stays on the gateway path.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers and go/internal/api Copilot tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "deviations",
      "claim": "Edge-case differences: error messages come from core and no longer quote upstream bodies; an HTTP-date Retry-After reaches the client as seconds; core lists /models once more after a restart or settings change; on the Messages path a number written like 1.0 is sent as 1.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/copilot_vertical.go and tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens; the providers iam.* budget moves from 59 to 58; every commit builds and passes tests; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
